{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-s737-wdrn-cukc-2nuq","published":"2026-11-20T00:26:33Z","modified":"2026-11-20T00:30:05.207023175Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-76101"],"summary":"keystore-go is a Go implementation of the Java KeyStore encoder and decoder. In 2.1.0 and earlier, keystore.Decode in…","details":"keystore-go is a Go implementation of the Java KeyStore encoder and decoder. In 2.1.0 and earlier, keystore.Decode in decoder.go does not check the error returned when reading the trailing SHA-1 integrity digest and bounds its comparison by the length of the digest actually read. If an attacker with write access removes the final 20-byte digest from a modified JKS file, the empty actual digest causes the comparison loop to execute zero times and Decode returns the parsed keystore without an error. For certificate-only stores using TrustedCertificateEntry values, this bypasses both tamper detection and password verification, allowing trusted CA certificates to be added or replaced without knowing the keystore password and potentially enabling interception or modification of TLS connections that trust the forged CA. This issue is fixed in version 3.0.0.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"cass-operator-dev","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/cass-operator-dev"},"versions":["1.31.0-r1","1.31.0-r2","1.31.0-r4","1.31.0-r5","1.32.0-r0","1.32.0-r1","1.32.0-r2","1.32.0-r3","1.32.0-r4","1.32.0-r5","1.32.0-r6","1.32.0-r7","1.32.0-r8","1.33.0-r0","1.33.1-r0","1.33.1-r1","1.33.1-r2","1.33.1-r3","1.33.1-r4"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-s737-wdrn-cukc-2nuq.json"}},{"package":{"name":"cass-operator-fips-dev","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/cass-operator-fips-dev"},"versions":["1.31.0-r1","1.31.0-r2","1.31.0-r4","1.31.0-r5","1.32.0-r0","1.32.0-r1","1.32.0-r2","1.32.0-r3","1.32.0-r4","1.32.0-r5","1.32.0-r6","1.32.